# results/ is NOT ignored: it holds the released data for the accompanying
# paper -- every model output, judge verdict, and human rating behind the
# reported numbers, plus results/archive/ with the earlier runs. Every figure
# and statistic in the paper is recomputed from these files by
# scripts/paper_stats.py, so they are part of the record, not build output.
# A fresh `run` overwrites results/ in place; commit deliberately or archive
# first.
